From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 05:28:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 10/28] isolate: expose context reuse decisions and cache state

Add bounded metrics for marked database-UDF validation decisions, context lookup and read-set validation outcomes, reusable cache lifecycle and occupancy, and scheduler affinity. Reuse the existing reusable initialization, module evaluation, isolate memory, and recreation signals instead of duplicating them.

Represent every new outcome, operation, context kind, and clear reason as a closed Rust enum. Emit affinity only after the selected worker accepts the request, give every found database context a terminal lookup outcome, clear scheduler advertisements before destroying cached contexts, and assert that the one-slot worker cache and scheduler mirror agree on complete context identity.

Preserve upstream one-slot last-save-wins behavior for nested reusable UDFs with explicit replacement accounting. On a reusable miss, prefer a same-client worker without a reusable context before allocating or stealing a worker, and cover that scheduler path with a focused regression test.

Keep labels application-independent. The maintained one-pool database and HTTP composition normally emits at most 26 counter plus two occupancy series, with a 30-counter hard bound including anomalous mutation lookup outcomes. Disable inactivity eviction for the five bounded counter vectors.

Document the one-slot cache shared by database and HTTP contexts, nested replacement, worker selection, metric semantics, executable-name prefixes, endpoint enablement, downstream metric export transformations, cardinality, runtime cost, and canary interpretation for self-hosted operators.
